+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The registry enforces the JSON Schema it advertises to providers before handing model input to a tool executor.
+
+## Contract
+
+- Invalid input returns a descriptive `ToolResponse` without invoking the executor: required fields, declared types and enum constraints are enforced, rejection text and logs identify paths and constraints without input values, valid inputs retain extra keys without coercion or defaults and execute exactly once, and unknown tool names still throw `Unknown tool: <name>` ([validated by: rejects malformed calls privately and passes accepted input through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L21)).
+- Static schemas compile during registration, an uncompilable schema throws an error naming the tool, and ten executions reuse the compiled schema without reading its schema properties again ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and reuses them across ten executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L61)).
+- Function-valued definitions resolve on each execution and validate against the current schema, caching compilation by resolved schema object rather than tool name ([validated by: validates each dynamic definition against its current schema and caches by schema object](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L86)).
+
+## Delivery requirements
+
+Use a runtime JSON Schema validator dependency; document the rejection contract in README.md, docs/adding-a-tool.md and .specify/spec.md, including extra-key preservation and the existing five-round retry bound. Keep execute's comment to one line pointing here. Publish a consumer-facing changelog and MINOR version migration note explaining that executors no longer receive malformed input. The existing orchestrator forwards returned tool results to the model, allowing a corrected retry within its round budget; output validation, authorization, timeout and rate limiting are outside this contract.
